# Tracer: exact rational powers through direct closed calculation.
# Before (fresh baseline release rejected both lines at Pow well-definedness):
# 8^(1/3)=2
# eval 8^(1/3)
# Former requirement: 1/3 $in Z; exit 1 and JSON success=false.
# Now: closed positive-rational bases admit rational exponents; exact roots
# followed by checked integer powers supply calculate and eval values.
# Boundary: irrational results are not approximated, checked overflow declines,
# and nonpositive bases with noninteger exponents remain outside this domain.
# Run: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/closed_rational_power_calculation.lit
# Regression/collector: tests/unit/execute/exact_rational_powers/tests.rs
# Each discarded sketch starts without facts from the preceding case.

sketch:
    8^(1/3)=2
sketch:
    16^(3/4)=8
sketch:
    (1/27)^(-1/3)=3
sketch:
    (8/27)^(2/3)=4/9
sketch:
    (4/9)^(1/2)=2/3
sketch:
    8^(2/6)=2
sketch:
    16^(0.75)=8
sketch:
    0.125^(1/3)=1/2
sketch:
    (81/16)^(3/4)=27/8
sketch:
    8^(-2/3)=1/4
sketch:
    8^(1/3)+1/3=7/3
sketch:
    (4/9)^(1/2)<3/4
sketch:
    8^(1/3) $in N+
sketch:
    eval 8^(1/3)
sketch:
    eval (4/9)^(1/2)
sketch:
    eval (1/27)^(-1/3)
